  "body": "This consists of three separate commits. Maybe the middle one should be squashed into one of the other two, or all three should be squashed, but at least for review purposes, they can be reviewed separately.\r\n\r\nThe reason I'm including integrity=\"\" and import() in the same PR is that making integrity=\"\" work allows for an easier refactoring that sets the stage for the import() work. So, the import() commit ends up being quite small, because the first commit does a lot of refactoring to set the stage for it.\r\n\r\nPreview at https://output-ypspnvheby.now.sh . Tests will probably come via Blink's implementation.\r\n\r\n/cc @whatwg/modules",
